UID:0f715000636285176889baa3263aef19@wheelingfeeling.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260830T145313Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260830T145313Z
SUMMARY:Jazz at the Stifel: Indestructible ft Roger Humphries
DTSTART:20260919T233000Z
DTEND:20260920T013000Z
DESCRIPTION:Pittsburgh based group Indestructible celebrates the music an
 d legacy of The Jazz Messengers\, performing compositions by Wayne Shorte
 r\, Lee Morgan\, Curtis Fuller\, Cedar Walton and others. The Jazz Messen
 gers was a jazz combo for over thirty-five years beginning in the early 1
 950’s as a collective\, and ending when the long- time leader and found
 ing drummer Art Blakey passed away in 1990. Indestructible is a jazz sext
 et led by trombonist Reggie Watkins and features master drummer Roger Hum
 phries. As a you musician\, Humphries was influenced and mentored by his 
 godfather and leader of The Jazz Messengers\, Art Blakey. “It is a spec
 ial treat to hear Roger in this musical context…”\, says Reggie Watki
 ns. “Given the history and connection between the two drummers\, Roger 
 Humphires is the perfect drummer to pay tribute to the great Art Blakey.
 ” Indestructible showcases some of the region’s most talented musicia
 ns like Michael Tomaro (sax)\, Tommy Lehman (trumpet)\, Howie Alexander (
 piano)\, Jordan McBride (bass)\, and several others. This high energy and
  relentlessly swinging group delivers blues infused improvisations\, mast
 erful arrangements and big band excitement. GET TICKETS HERE or call 304-
 242-7700\nSchedule note: One Day Only\nCategories: Music\nSource: https:/
 /wheelingcvb.com/events/jazz-at-the-stifel-indestructible-ft-roger-humphr
 ies/
LOCATION:Oglebay Institute's Stifel Fine Arts Center\, 1330 National Road
 \, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/jazz-at-the-stifel-indestructible-ft-r
 oger-humphries/
CLASS:PUBLIC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
