BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c722e3b4425e795b80eb262c2fc6cc7d@wheelingfeeling.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260830T145313Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260830T145313Z
SUMMARY:Whiskey Myers w/ The Ransom Brothers
DTSTART:20261006T230000Z
DTEND:20261007T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:Whiskey Myers has carved out a reputation as one of the most 
 dynamic and authentic bands in modern American music. Since emerging from
  East Texas in 2007\, the six-piece has built a devoted fanbase through r
 elentless touring\, playing nearly 3\,000 live shows and selling out icon
 ic venues including Red Rocks Amphitheatre and the Ryman Auditorium. Know
 n for their signature blend of Southern rock\, country\, blues\, and hard
 -driving rock and roll\, Whiskey Myers has amassed more than 4.1 billion 
 streams\, sold over 2.7 million albums\, and earned nine RIAA Gold\, Plat
 inum\, and multi-Platinum certifications as an independent band. Their mu
 sic has been featured in hit television series including Yellowstone\, La
 ndman\, SEAL Team\, and What/If\, further expanding their reach beyond th
 e stage. Led by Cody Cannon alongside Cody Tate\, John Jeffers\, Jamey Gl
 eaves\, Tony Kent\, and Jeff Hogg\, the band has shared stages with some 
 of music’s biggest names\, including opening for The Rolling Stones at 
 Chicago’s Soldier Field. Renowned for their electrifying live performan
 ces and genre-defying sound\, Whiskey Myers continues to push boundaries 
 while staying true to the blue-collar grit and authenticity that have def
 ined them from the beginning. WITH SPECIAL GUEST - THE RANSOM BROTHERS Th
 e Ransom Brothers are Austin-based Southern country rockers pushing the b
 oundaries of Americana. Fronted by Sean McHargue and Daniel Solis\, the f
 ull band delivers layered instrumentation\, heartfelt storytelling\, powe
 rful vocal harmonies\, and high-octane energy that scales from intimate v
 enues to festival stages. Their journey has taken them from local honky-t
 onks to supporting Whiskey Myers\, Drake White\, Chase Rice\, Band of Hea
 thens\, and Southall\, steadily building a devoted following across Texas
  and beyond. With lyrics drawn from personal experiences and everyday lif
 e\, their music blends outlaw country grit and blues-driven rock\, creati
 ng a sound that's as rich and diverse as the Texan landscape itself\, and
  connections that fans feel deep in the soul. With their upcoming full-le
 ngth album\, The Ransom Brothers showcase an evolved sonic identity that 
 bridges country\, rock\, and Americana with raw emotion and captivating p
 erformances. Produced by Gordy Quist (Band of Heathens) and mixed by Gram
 my-winner Steve Christensen (Khruangbin\, Steve Earle)\, it is sonically 
 bolder than their past work\, pairing heartfelt storytelling and a soarin
 g country-rock groove with Austin's Americana and red dirt roots. This re
 lease marks a new chapter for the band and sets the stage for their rise 
 as one of Texas' most compelling new voices in Southern country rock.\nSc
 hedule note: One Day Only\nCategories: Capitol Theatre\, Music\nSource: h
 ttps://wheelingcvb.com/events/whiskey-myers-w-the-ransom-brothers/
LOCATION:Capitol Theatre\, 1015 Main Street\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/whiskey-myers-w-the-ransom-brothers/
CLASS:PUBLIC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
