BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9837d10c5955f7a2a0a656ec06a43a60@wheelingfeeling.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260830T145313Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260830T145313Z
SUMMARY:Daughtry: 20 Years Unplugged Tour w/ Ryan Purdz
DTSTART:20261028T000000Z
DTEND:20261028T020000Z
DESCRIPTION:Formed in 2006\, the Grammy Award®-nominated\, multi-platinu
 m rock band Daughtry has remained a dominant force for nearly two decades
 . Fronted by powerhouse vocalist Chris Daughtry\, the band has sold more 
 than 11 million records worldwide\, earned four Grammy nominations\, rece
 ived American Music Awards\, and achieved multiple Billboard chart-topper
 s\, including three No. 1 rock singles. Entering a bold new chapter with 
 their latest albums\, Dearly Beloved and Shock to the System\, Daughtry d
 elivers a harder-edged\, high-impact statement that reaffirms their evolu
 tion and staying power—proving they’re not just part of the rock conv
 ersation but are still driving it. Celebrating 20 years of chart-topping 
 hits\, Daughtry is bringing the 20 Years Unplugged Tour to Wheeling this 
 fall. WITH SPECIAL GUEST - RYAN PERDZ Ryan Perdz is a 24-year-old singer\
 , songwriter\, and multi-instrumentalist from Buffalo\, NY. Raised on his
  grandparents’ family farm\, he began teaching himself guitar at age te
 n and expanded into bass\, violin\, and mandolin\, developing a hands-on 
 approach to songwriting and arrangement. Influenced by artists such as Ni
 rvana\, Chris Cornell\, Red Hot Chili Peppers\, and Led Zeppelin\, Perdz 
 channels the emotional weight of 90s rock through a modern lens\, balanci
 ng grit with melody. His music often explores isolation\, self-doubt\, an
 d perseverance\, delivered with a clarity that feels lived-in rather than
  ornamental. After independently releasing multiple singles and his First
  Sight EP an racking up tens of millions of views across social media\, P
 erdz cultivated a loyal audience through consistent self-directed output.
  In 2025\, he signed with Big Machine Rock and began recording his debut 
 full-length album. His growing catalogue of original music has generated 
 millions of streams\, and his audience continues to expand across digital
  platforms as he releases singles from his forthcoming debut\, including 
 “Sour” and “Heavy Eyes.” As he prepares to unveil his debut album
 \, Ryan Perdz stands positioned at the forefront of a new generation of r
 ock artists shaped by both digital culture and classic influences.\nSched
 ule note: One Day Only\nCategories: Capitol Theatre\, Music\nSource: http
 s://wheelingcvb.com/events/daughtry-20-years-unplugged-tour-w-ryan-purdz/
LOCATION:Capitol Theatre\, 1015 Main Street\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
