BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:179f74c30af770acacaa79c0fd5b8889@wheelingfeeling.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260830T145313Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260830T145313Z
SUMMARY:The Gift Christmas Concert
DTSTART:20261205T000000Z
DTEND:20261205T020000Z
DESCRIPTION:Come experience the magic of Christmas as music fills your he
 art and lifts your spirit. Attendees of The Gift can expect to be captiva
 ted by a mix of traditional Christmas songs and contemporary holiday hits
  that will evoke the magic and wonder of the season. As the lights twinkl
 e\, soul stirring performances and heartfelt storytelling bring the timel
 ess message of the Christmas story to life. Plus\, a special appearance b
 y Santa Claus himself! New this year! Enjoy simple All-In Pricing with $5
 0 Reserved Seating and $40 General Admission (fees included). Plus\, a po
 rtion of the net proceeds from every ticket sold will benefit the Thomas 
 Auto Centers Military Freedom Tree\, helping honor and support our milita
 ry community. MUSICAL LINEUP JO ANN JONES Jo Ann is an established Countr
 y/Gospel vocalist and recording artist. Her Christmas CD The Gift has cap
 tured the essence of Christmas through her soulful vocals and uplifting l
 yrics. Jo Ann is known for sharing the stage with many iconic artists as 
 a member of Jamboree USA and Jamboree in the Hills. Her Christmas CD The 
 Gift is available on iTunes. ROGER HOARD Roger is the co-music director o
 f The Gift concert. He is perhaps the most recognizable and respected tal
 ent to ever play guitar. Roger has performed with the great Chet Atkins. 
 He was the guitar instructor to the valley’s own Brad Paisley. Roger wa
 s the music director of Jamboree USA and has been band mates with several
  formidable bands including\, The Other Brothers who played at the Grand 
 Ole Opry\, The 1170 Band\, house band of Jamboree USA and currently of Ho
 ard and Jones. JAMIE PECK Jamie is the co-music director of The Gift conc
 ert. Jamie is an Emmy Award winning composer and musician\, working in te
 levision and radio. Jamie joins the musicians on keyboard\, saxophone\, o
 rgan\, and flute. Jamie is the owner\, engineer\, and producer at Jamie P
 eck Productions in Wheeling\, WV. DAN JONES Dan Jones is a multi-talented
  musician and vocalist. His talents on guitar\, fiddle\, mandolin\, and h
 armonica add more layers to this musical celebration. Dan is a premier me
 mber of the dynamic duo of Hoard and Jones. MARK STATLER Mark is a Countr
 y and Gospel singer and performer. He has recorded several CDs and has pe
 rformed throughout the Ohio Valley. Mark is serving as the lead pastor of
  the Church of Christ of Christian Disciples in Carrollton\, Ohio. He is 
 well known for his heartwarming delivery of Christian and inspirational m
 usic. Mark has performed at Jamboree USA and has opened for many country 
 music favorites. SHIRAH BROTHERS The Gift welcomes the Shirah Brothers fr
 om Cookeville\, Tennessee. Jake and Josh Shirah and Samuel McIntyre are t
 he members of this dynamic Southern Gospel vocal group. They have perform
 ed across the country and have an extensive tour schedule. The Shirah Bro
 thers are thrilled to share their Christmas music and spread the joyous m
 essage of the season. SANDY LUSCO HUFFMAN Sandy is a musician\, singer-so
 ngwriter who has impressively recorded eleven albums featuring many of he
 r original songs. Her heartfelt lyrics are sure to capture the warmth of 
 the Christmas season. DENNIS CRAIG Dennis joins the group as Bass guitari
 st. He has performed with The Other Brothers on the Grand Ole Opry stage 
 and at Jamboree USA and Jamboree in the Hills. Dennis has played for Char
 lie Pride\, Kathy Mattea\, Ray Price\, and Steve Wariner. THE RON RETZER 
 TRIO The Ron Retzer Ttrio features Jennifer Galowina\, Bob Wolfe\, and Ro
 n Retzer. The trio have been singing together since 2014 and specialize i
 n Christian and popular music. The soaring vocal style of this group is a
  special blessing during the Christmas season. CHAD SMITH Chad joins the 
 group as vocalist and percussionist\, specializing in a variety of percus
 sion instruments. Chad worked many years as Brad Paisley’s drummer and 
 has performed at The Wheeling Jamboree and Jamboree in the Hills. Chad is
  currently the drummer for MSM\, the Miller\, Smith\, Mazure band. TOM BR
 EIDING Tom Breiding is a musical spokesperson for the United Mine Workers
  of America\, the 2022 Hazel Dickens Art-Maker Award Recipient designated
  by the West Virginia Mine Wars Museum\, and he is Director of the Cliffo
 rd M. Lewis Appalachian Institute at Wheeling University. This year Tom c
 elebrates his 10th year as invited artist to the annual Woody Gutherie Fo
 lk Festival. His work has taken him all over the U.S. including his home 
 state of WV. JERRY WENGER Jerry Wenger is returning to The Gift Concert. 
 He has pastored in the Ohio Valley for the past 38 years and is currently
  serving at Mt. Pleasant Friends Church. He has sung country and gospel m
 usic his whole life and is a published songwriter. He was a founding memb
 er of the contemporary Christian band called Narrow Road that performed t
 hroughout the Ohio Valley. CHARLIE MCVAY A talented steel guitar player a
 nd a veteran 1170 band performer\, renowned for his significant contribut
 ions to the original WWVA Jamboree USA\, where he captivated audiences fo
 r 23 memorable years. LIAM PECK Liam is a vocalist with a charismatic sta
 ge presence who connects with the audience and is a promising up and comi
 ng talent. DUSTIN KINSEY Emcee\nSchedule note: One Day Only\nCategories: 
 Capitol Theatre\, Holiday\, Music\nSource: https://wheelingcvb.com/events
 /the-gift-christmas-concert/
LOCATION:Capitol Theatre\, 1015 Main Street\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/the-gift-christmas-concert/
CLASS:PUBLIC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
