UID:ebc39d75eb726bf30a26ad3b6485d974@wheelingfeeling.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260830T145313Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260830T145313Z
SUMMARY:Colin Mochrie & Brad Sherwood: Asking For Trouble
DTSTART:20270109T003000Z
DTEND:20270109T023000Z
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for an evening of sidesplitting laughter as Colin M
 ochrie and Brad Sherwood\, the dynamic duo from TV's "Whose Line is it An
 yway?\," take the stage in a one-night-only uproarious live show\, Colin 
 Mochrie & Brad Sherwood: Asking for Trouble. Armed with their lightning-f
 ast wits\, Mochrie & Sherwood transform the audience’s suggestions into
  an unpredictable evening of non-stop comedy gold. No script? No problem!
  “Asking For Trouble” is a wild rollercoaster ride of hilarity\, wher
 e two improv legends prove they are still the best in the business. ABOUT
  COLIN MOCHRIE Scotland\, that craggy\, majestic\, malt whiskeyed land\, 
 has spawned many myths besides the Loch Ness Monster. One such legend is 
 Colin Mochrie (Hilaritycus smoothius). A migratory creature that left his
  birthplace for the Great White North (Canada)\, Colin learned his theatr
 ical craft through repeated behavioral rituals at Studio 58 located in th
 e mountain nestled\, sparkling jewel of the Northwest\, Vancouver\, Briti
 sh Columbia. A hard-working\, imaginative mammal\, Colin used his chamele
 on-like skills to blend in with others of his ilk\, never being noticed\,
  until noted anthropologists Dan Patterson and Mark Leveson discovered hi
 m at the Toronto Second City. Moving him to the Whose Line is it Anyway I
 nstitute in historical and damp London\, England\, Patterson and Leveson 
 slowly groomed Colin till he became international sensation. Working with
  Drew Carey at the U.S based institute of the same name\, only increased 
 interest in the reclusive beast. ABOUT BRAD SHERWOOD As a young hatchling
 \, Brad Sherwood (Cranius gigantum)\, fled the ice plains of Chicago for 
 the arid expanse of the Rocky Mountains\, where he settled at the epicent
 er of art and coyote sculptures\, Santa Fe New Mexico. Weaned on green ch
 iles and isolation\, he became a savant of self-amusement. Years later\, 
 he hopped a hobo train to the Pacific Ocean where he searched for people 
 willing to employ someone with an abnormally large skull. Eventually\, he
  was plucked from the Venice Beach Freak Show by a band of improvising gy
 psies who passed him from troupe to troupe\, until he was sold into servi
 tude to some British Choreographer/Pirates. They\, in turn\, sold him to 
 a British improv TV show\, where he was hired to teach Canadians how to b
 e funny. Now\, he is ward and caretaker of his least successful pupil\, C
 olin Mochrie. Brad is given a stipend from the Canadian government to kee
 p Colin from hurting himself or livestock. As part of Colin's therapy\, B
 rad tours with him in an improvised stage performance that helps creative
 ly channel Mochrie's delusions.\nSchedule note: One Day Only\nCategories:
  Capitol Theatre\, Comedy\nSource: https://wheelingcvb.com/events/colin-m
 ochrie-brad-sherwood-asking-for-trouble/
LOCATION:Capitol Theatre\, 1015 Main Street\, Wheeling\, WV 26003
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/colin-mochrie-brad-sherwood-asking-for
 -trouble/
CLASS:PUBLIC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
