SUMMARY:The People's University: America 250 - Revolution & Constitution
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260813
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260814
DESCRIPTION:Lifelong Learning at Your Library! In 1951\, the Ohio County 
 Public Library's head librarian\, Virginia Ebeling\, referenced British h
 istorian Thomas Carlyle\, who said\, “the public library is a People’
 s University\,” when she initiated a new adult education program with t
 hat name. Miss Ebeling charged the Library with the responsibility of rea
 ching “as many people in the community as possible.” In keeping with 
 that tradition of public libraries as sanctuaries of free learning for al
 l people\, the Ohio County Public Library revived the series in 2010. The
  People’s University is a free program for adults who wish to continue 
 their education in the liberal arts. It features courses—taught by expe
 rts in each subject—that enable patrons to pursue their goal of lifelon
 g learning in classic subjects such as history\, philosophy\, and literat
 ure. Patrons may attend as many classes as they wish. There are no tests 
 of other requirements and all programs are free and open to the public. A
 nd now you can watch online too! 2026 America 250: Revolution & Constitut
 ion ➤ Download a .pdf file of the brochure or stop at the Library to pi
 ck up a paper copy CLASS SCHEDULE: Class 1: Thursday\, June 25 — 7PM - 
 The Meaning of Freedom (1763-1775) Class 2: Thursday\, July 2 — 7PM - I
 ndependence Declared\, 1775-1776 Class 3: Thursday\, July 9 — 7PM - The
  Double Sevens - 1777 Class 4: Thursday\, July 16 — 7PM - The Year of t
 he French - 1778 Class 5: Thursday\, July 23 — 7PM - The Battle of Camd
 en - 1779-1780 Class 6: Thursday\, July 30 — 7PM - Siege and Surrender 
 -1781-1782 Class 7\, Thursday\, August 6 — 7PM - Foundations of Freedom
  - 1783-1789 Class 8: Thursday\, August 13 — NOON - Finale: "A Republic
 --if You Can Keep It." Readings from the Declaration of Independence and 
 Constitution What to expect at People's University: America 250: Revoluti
 on & Constitution?https://www.facebook.com/peoplesuniversityOCPL Classes 
 will also be livestreamed and will be available on the Lunch With Books F
 acebook and YouTube pages during and after the live event.\nSchedule note
 : Every Thursday\nCategories: Educational\, Free Events\nSource: https://
 wheelingcvb.com/events/the-peoples-university-2026-america-250-revolution
 -constitution/
LOCATION:Ohio County Public Library\, 52 16th Street\, Wheeling\, WV 2600
 3
URL:https://wheelingcvb.com/events/the-peoples-university-2026-america-25
 0-revolution-constitution/
CLASS:PUBLIC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
